  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "Fixed: `session_ttl_expired` now works with timezone-aware timestamps, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` passes.\n\n**The bug:** in `session_ttl.py`, only `now` had its timezone removed (`.replace(tzinfo=None)`) while `created` kept its `+00:00`. Subtracting a timestamp with no timezone from one that has one raises `TypeError`.\n\n**The fix:** I parse both timestamps the same way and dropped the `.replace(tzinfo=None)` call. Two timestamps with timezones now subtract correctly, even across different offsets. Two timestamps without timezones still work as before. `format_expiry_message` is untouched.\n\nI also checked by hand that 30 seconds of elapsed time across `+00:00` and `+01:00` counts as not expired, and that timestamps without timezones still work.\n\nThe formatter still flags the file because of the existing long `ttl_seconds` validation line. I didn't change it, to keep the fix minimal.\n\nDONE: Parsed now_iso without stripping tzinfo so timezone-aware timestamps subtract correctly; public test passes.",
