      "final_message": "`service2.compute_fee(1000, \"gold\")` returns **480**. I got this by tracing the code and confirmed it by running the call.\n\n1. `compute_fee` imports only `pricing` and `discounts`. Nothing imports `decoy_tax.py` or `decoy_shipping.py`, so they don't affect the result.\n2. `pricing.base_fee(1000)` is 500 + 1000 // 10 = 600.\n3. `discounts.apply_discount(600, \"gold\")` applies the 20% gold discount: 600 \u2212 (600 \u00d7 20) // 100 = 600 \u2212 120 = 480.\n\nANSWER: 480",
